From: AX6 EDMA correctness audit
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] edma_v1: use dma_mapping_error() instead of !dma check

The Linux DMA API requires dma_mapping_error(dev, dma) to test for
mapping failures. DMA address 0 can be a valid address on some
platforms, and error values are not guaranteed to be 0. The current
code uses `if (!dma)` which is incorrect.

Fixes F1 from AX6 cross-audit 2026-07-26.
⚠ PATCH NEEDS BUILD-TREE VERIFICATION: line numbers and exact file
  paths must be confirmed against the extracted QSDK EDMA v1 source.

--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_data_plane.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_data_plane.c
@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ static int edma_tx_packet(struct sk_buff
 	preheader = edma_get_preheader_len();
 	dma = dma_map_single(dev, skb->data, skb_headlen(skb) + preheader,
 			     DMA_TO_DEVICE);
-	if (!dma)
+	if (dma_mapping_error(dev, dma))
 		goto drop;

 	/* ... TX descriptor programming ... */
@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ static int edma_rx_refill(struct edma_hw
 	dma = dma_map_single(dev, skb->data, edma_hw.rx_buf_size,
 			     DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
-	if (!dma) {
+	if (dma_mapping_error(dev, dma)) {
 		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
